*PaperDimension Nagagata3/Nagagata3 (120 x 235mm): "340 666"

*% Anything the firmware has no code for is sent as a custom page: the
*% filter then emits DMPAPER 0 plus the width/height in 1/600 inch.
*CustomPageSize True: "pop pop pop <</PageSize [5 -2 roll] /ImagingBBox null>> setpagedevice"
*ParamCustomPageSize Width: 1 points 212 618
*ParamCustomPageSize Height: 2 points 419 1021
*ParamCustomPageSize WidthOffset: 3 points 0 0
*ParamCustomPageSize HeightOffset: 4 points 0 0
*ParamCustomPageSize Orientation: 5 int 1 1

*% cupsMediaType is what the filter actually reads; the option string is
*% never consulted for the media type.
*OpenUI *MediaType/Paper Type: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10.0 AnySetup *MediaType
*DefaultMediaType: Plain
*MediaType Plain/Plain: "<</MediaType(Plain)/cupsMediaType 1>>setpagedevice"
*% The vendor PPD calls this one "Kleenex". The wire value (263) is what the
*% device cares about; the keyword is ours.
*MediaType Thin/Thin paper: "<</MediaType(Thin paper)/cupsMediaType 263>>setpagedevice"
*MediaType Thick/Thick: "<</MediaType(Thick)/cupsMediaType 289>>setpagedevice"
*MediaType Cardstock/Cardstock: "<</MediaType(Card)/cupsMediaType 286>>setpagedevice"
*MediaType Label/Label: "<</MediaType(Labels)/cupsMediaType 261>>setpagedevice"
*MediaType Envelope/Envelope: "<</MediaType(Envelope)/cupsMediaType 259>>setpagedevice"
*MediaType Transparency/Transparency: "<</MediaType(Transparency)/cupsMediaType 2>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *MediaType

*% Any media type other than Plain forces the manual tray, whatever is
*% selected here.
*OpenUI *InputSlot/Paper Source: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 20.0 AnySetup *InputSlot
*DefaultInputSlot: Auto
*InputSlot Auto/Automatic: "<</MediaPosition 0>>setpagedevice"
*InputSlot ManualFeed/Manual Feeder: "<</MediaPosition 1>>setpagedevice"
*InputSlot AutoFeed/Automatic Feeder: "<</MediaPosition 2>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *InputSlot

*% There is no hardware duplex on this model.  Manual duplex prints the
*% front sides, pauses the engine and then prints the backs in reverse.
*OpenUI *ManualDuplex/Manual Duplex: Boolean
*OrderDependency: 15.0 AnySetup *ManualDuplex
*DefaultManualDuplex: False
*ManualDuplex False/Off: "<</ManualDuplex false>>setpagedevice"
*ManualDuplex True/On: "<</ManualDuplex true>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *ManualDuplex
*CloseGroup: PaperGroup

*OpenGroup: Graphics/Print Quality
*% Both settings put 600x600 in the raster header: at "1200 DPI" the filter
*% switches to two bits per pixel and doubles the JBIG image width.
*OpenUI *DPI1200/Resolution: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10.0 AnySetup *DPI1200
*DefaultDPI1200: False
*DPI1200 False/600 DPI: "<</HWResolution [600 600]/cupsBitsPerColor 8/cupsBitsPerPixel 8/cupsColorSpace 0>>setpagedevice"
*DPI1200 True/1200 DPI: "<</HWResolution [600 600]/cupsBitsPerColor 8/cupsBitsPerPixel 8/cupsColorSpace 0>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *DPI1200

*OpenUI *Density/Density: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 50.0 AnySetup *Density
*DefaultDensity: 2
*Density 0/Lighter: ""
*Density 2/Normal: ""
*Density 4/Darker: ""
*CloseUI: *Density

*% Toner save has no bit of its own here: it is the minimum density.
*OpenUI *TonerMode/Toner Save: Boolean
*OrderDependency: 55.0 AnySetup *TonerMode
*DefaultTonerMode: False
*TonerMode False/Off: ""
*TonerMode True/On: ""
*CloseUI: *TonerMode

*OpenUI *NegativePrint/Negative Print: Boolean
*OrderDependency: 56.0 AnySetup *NegativePrint
*DefaultNegativePrint: False
*NegativePrint False/Off: ""
*NegativePrint True/On: ""
*CloseUI: *NegativePrint

*OpenUI *ImageRotation/Rotate 180 degrees: Boolean
*OrderDependency: 57.0 AnySetup *ImageRotation
*DefaultImageRotation: False
*ImageRotation False/Off: ""
*ImageRotation True/On: ""
*CloseUI: *ImageRotation
*CloseGroup: Graphics

*% Kept from the vendor PPD, which declares the same pair: a negative page is
*% mostly toner, and printing it at the toner-save density gives a grey mess
*% rather than a saving.
*UIConstraints: *NegativePrint True *TonerMode True
*UIConstraints: *TonerMode True *NegativePrint True
*% Manual duplex needs paper the engine can take twice.
*UIConstraints: *ManualDuplex True *MediaType Thin
*UIConstraints: *ManualDuplex True *MediaType Thick
*UIConstraints: *ManualDuplex True *MediaType Cardstock
*UIConstraints: *ManualDuplex True *MediaType Label
*UIConstraints: *ManualDuplex True *MediaType Envelope
*UIConstraints: *ManualDuplex True *MediaType Transparency
*UIConstraints: *MediaType Thin *ManualDuplex True
*UIConstraints: *MediaType Thick *ManualDuplex True
*UIConstraints: *MediaType Cardstock *ManualDuplex True
*UIConstraints: *MediaType Label *ManualDuplex True
*UIConstraints: *MediaType Envelope *ManualDuplex True
*UIConstraints: *MediaType Transparency *ManualDuplex True

*% ==== End of PPD ====
